<h1>Jessica Maronto</h1>
<p>City traffic signal repair worker. Candidate for mayor of Chicago, on the ballot February 23, 2027.</p>
<p>Repairs traffic signals for the Chicago Department of Transportation. Filed on the last day, told reporters her petitions would fall short, and does not plan to campaign actively.</p>
<p><a href="https://marontoforchicago.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign website (marontoforchicago.com)</a></p>
<h2>Campaign money</h2>
<ul>
<li>Committee: Committee to Elect Jessica Maronto for Mayor</li>
<li>Raised: $33K</li>
<li>Spent: $3,853</li>
<li>Cash on hand: $29K</li>
<li>Since the committee formed, through Sept. 30, 2026. Mostly loans from the candidate. <a href="https://elections.il.gov/CampaignDisclosure/CommitteeDetail.aspx?id=41339" rel="nofollow noopener">Source</a></li>
</ul>
<p>Money figures are each committee&#39;s quarterly reports to the Illinois State Board of Elections: spent is total expenditures from January 1 to September 30, 2026 (or since the committee formed), cash is funds available on September 30.</p>
<h2>Support</h2>
<p>Not listed in the ChicagoSpeaks poll, Sept. 2026 (Mansueto Institute / NORC). 0.0 points of support per $1 million spent.</p>
<h2>What they would do</h2>
<ul>
<li>Says the campaign&#39;s energy goes to its projects and mission rather than to campaigning. <q>we&#39;re focusing our efforts on the projects and mission</q> (<a href="https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/chicago-mayor-election-candidates-2027-petitions-filed/" rel="nofollow noopener">CBS Chicago, Oct. 2026</a>)</li>
<li>A city worker&#39;s run for the top job, funded mostly out of pocket.</li>
</ul>
<h2>AI summary</h2>
<h3>Main points</h3>
<p>The pitch: A city worker who repairs traffic signals, running without an active campaign.</p>
<p>Not published: No platform on the record beyond the campaign&#39;s stated focus on its projects and mission.</p>
<h3>Next to the others</h3>
<p>Only Maronto: A current city employee, and the only candidate who says she is not campaigning.</p>
<p>Self-funded: Maronto, Wilson, Holberg, and Nee lent their own campaigns money.</p>
<h2>On money</h2>
<p>No position on taxes or the budget on the record.</p>
<h2>Pizza</h2>
<p>No position on record.</p>
